josephus-josip-pilipic|baptism|1768|notes/karlobag-the-index-calls-them-piberich.md|Karlobag, 11 March 1768 — INDEX ONLY, «Josephum Piberich», father «Jacobi Piberich», mother «Catharina»; ark 1:1:QKMX-YX3G. «Piberich» is the index's misreading and occurs nowhere else at Karlobag; the same couple are «Pillopich» in 1758 and «Pillepich» in 1762 and 1765
marija-milka-kalanj|baptism|1888|notes/the-zeros-were-not-all-zeros.md|Ledenice, 16 May 1888 — INDEX ONLY, «Marija Milka», parents «Luka Kalanj» and «Kata Kalanj»; ark 1:1:XQM9-8KKX. The tree carries the year alone and cites the image; the index supplies the day. The mother is Kata Miletić in the tree — the index has given her the father's surname
maria-catharina-oreskovic-oreskovic|baptism|1835|site/src/pages/frontier.astro|Otočac, 8 Sep 1835, Dubrava 29 — her own baptism, the entry both her parents were already credited from: «Marcus Oreskovich, adoptatus Sekula» and «Lucia uxor ejus nata Sekula». The rule says a baptism counts for the child AND both parents; the parents had rows and the child did not
antonija-tonka-perpic-prpic|baptism|1859|notes/the-household-was-swept-and-she-was-left-out.md|Krivi Put, born 12 May 1859, baptised 15 May 1859 — INDEX ONLY, «Antonia Perpić», father «Joannis Perpić», mother «Luciæ Perpić»; ark 1:1:XQM9-6NQ4. AGREES WITH THE TREE TO THE DAY, and the three-day gap to baptism is ordinary for this parish. The index gives the mother the father's surname, so it does not supply ahnentafel 15's maiden name
milka-lucia-papic|baptism|1886|site/src/pages/milka.astro|Senj baptisms Str. 122 entry 96, READ FROM THE IMAGE — «Milka Lucia», zakonita, born 9 October 1886, baptised 17 October; father «Josip Papić, trhonoša», mother «Tonka rođ. Prpić»; godparents Josip Glavičić, trhonoša, and Ivka Filipović. The register writes the birth «1886, 9/10». The margin was annotated at her death: «Uvidom u matičnu knjigu umrlih opć. Senj str. 280. red. br. 37. umrla dana 7.9.1971», endorsed 30.9.1971
milka-lucia-papic|marriage|1907|site/src/pages/milka.astro|Senj marriages p. 294 entry 30 — 4 studenoga 1907, «Milka Papić, radnica u tvornici duhana», born 9 October 1886, to «Zvonimir M. Vukelić, gostioničarski pomoćnik». Re-read at 5,812 x 4,273 on 13 September 2026, image 299, ark 3:1:3QS7-L99X-175J. Her birth is written «9/X» here — a SECOND register entry, thirteen years and a different hand later, and it says October too
#
# Image reads this archive had PUBLISHED and never recorded here, recovered
# 20 September 2026 by holding corrections.json and the site's own pages against
# readings.psv. See notes/the-evidence-file-under-reported-the-archive.md
ljubomir-blazevic|marriage|1920|site/src/pages/marriage-1920.astro|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) p. 366 entry 41 — 8 prosinca 1920 at Senj, read from the image and re-read at full resolution, ark 3:1:3QSQ-G99X-17M7. Dispensed by the ordinariate, act no. 3371 of 4 December
milka-lucia-papic|marriage|1920|site/src/pages/marriage-1920.astro|Senj marriages (Vjenčani) p. 366 entry 41 — her second marriage, 8 prosinca 1920, to Ljubomir Blažević; ark 3:1:3QSQ-G99X-17M7
juraj-georgius-jure-blazevic|marriage-of-child|1920|site/src/pages/marriage-1920.astro|named as the groom's father, «Juraj Blažević», and annotated «mrt.» — deceased — which puts his death before December 1920. Senj marriages p. 366 entry 41
tereza-zubrinic-zubrinic|marriage-of-child|1920|site/src/pages/marriage-1920.astro|named as the groom's mother, «Tereza r. Žubrinić», annotated «mrt.» in the same entry. Senj marriages p. 366 entry 41
antonija-blazevic|marriage|1918|site/src/data/corrections.json|Senj marriages p. 348 no. 5 — her own entry of 1 April 1918, written from her baptismal certificate, giving her birth as «1884 12/5» where the tree says 17 May. Entered «nadglednica u tvornici duhana» — supervisor, not a floor worker — daughter of Pavao Blažević and Marija r. Tomljanović, «poljodjelci iz župe Krmpote»
katica-blazevic|marriage|1919|site/src/data/corrections.json|Senj marriages p. 355 no. 18 — her marriage to Viktor Matijević, 12 May 1919, entered «radnica u tvornici duhana», of Krmpote, daughter of Pavao Blažević and Marija r. Tomljanović. Confirms the tree's 19 October 1885
terezija-tereza-blazevic|marriage|1913|site/src/data/corrections.json|Senj marriages p. 326 no. 23 — her marriage to Josip Nagoda, 5 October 1913, entered «radnica u tvornici duhana u Senju, iz župe sv. Jakov Krmpote»; parents Pavao Blažević and Marija r. Tomljanović, «poljodjelci» of the same parish. Confirms the tree's 23 October 1888
tereza-papic|death|1903|site/src/data/corrections.json|Senj deaths p. 162 no. 51 — «Papić Tereza, kći nadničara Franje i Kate Papić, 4 7/12 god, Scarlatina», died 2 June 1903 and buried at sv. Vid the next day. The register names the father the tree leaves blank
anka-blazevic|grave|1953|site/src/data/corrections.json|The Kosina grave at Senj — «KOSINA · KRIŽAN · ANKA», Anka «✻?.X.1893 †6.IX.1953», where the tree carried only the year. The same stone gives her husband Pavao «pog. 8.X.1943 — Nevina žrtva zračnog napadaja na Senj». Her birth month on the stone is cracked and ivy-covered and is NOT legible enough to contradict her 1919 marriage entry
ana-kalanj|baptism|1894|site/src/data/corrections.json|Novi Vinodolski baptisms str. 278 no. 71 — «Ana, kći zakonita» of «Martin Kalanj Josipov, žena mu Marija rodj. Peričić»; born 5 November 1894, baptised 11 November 1894. The patronymic «Josipov» is the find: it matches the tree's Josip Kalanj independently of the tree. Read at 3x, where the mother's surname reads Peričić and not the Crnić it seemed at page scale
franciska-kalanj|baptism|1896|site/src/data/corrections.json|Novi Vinodolski baptisms — born 29 July 1896, register scan held at 2,953 px. One of four consecutive siblings whose baptisms were sitting unattached in the family's own photo library
zora-kalanj|baptism|1898|site/src/data/corrections.json|Novi Vinodolski baptisms — born 4 March 1898, register scan held at 2,953 px. Her godparents are entered «Josip i Ana Defrancesco» — the child's aunt and uncle, which is what proves Ana and Martin Kalanj are sister and brother
ivan-kalanj|baptism|1900|site/src/data/corrections.json|Novi Vinodolski baptisms — born 3 January 1900, register scan held at 2,953 px. The fourth of the four loose sibling scans
anica-ana-anna-kalanj|baptism|1864|site/src/data/corrections.json|Her 1864 baptism — born 3 January 1864 — enters her parents as «Josephus Kalanj» and «Rosalia nata Perković» at Klenovica 22, the same couple the tree gives her brother Martin, AND as «Brinjensis parochiae ruricolae» — country people of the parish of BRINJE. That line was read, transcribed and then not acted on: every search this archive has run for the Kalanji has been on the coast
rozalia-kalanj|baptism|1893|notes/novi-vinodolski-is-indexed-to-1899.md|Novi Vinodolski, baptised 5 August 1893 — INDEX ONLY, «Rozalia Kalanj», father «Martin Kalanj», mother «Maria Peričić»; ark 1:1:XQMQ-QY3Q. The FIFTH child of this household and the one whose scan is NOT in the family's photo library, where the other four sat. The tree gives her birth as 4 July 1893, so the index puts a month between birth and baptism where her siblings' entries put days — unexplained, and a reason to open the page
anka-blazevic|marriage|1919|notes/the-kosina-are-filed-under-senia.md|Senj — INDEX ONLY, her marriage to «Pavao Kosina» b.1894, of «Martin Kosina» and «Andjelika Boras»; she is entered b.1893, of «Juraj Blažević» and «Tereza Žubrinić»; ark 1:1:X9D5-MWXX. Hungary, Croatia-Slavonia, Marriages 1678-1927. The index confirms the join to ahnentafel 4 and 5 independently of the tree
angelika-boras|baptism-of-child|1891|notes/the-kosina-are-filed-under-senia.md|named as mother, «Angelica Boras», at the baptism of her son Antonius Joannes Kosina — born 13 May 1891, baptised 15 June 1891; ark 1:1:X9DP-3YJQ. INDEX ONLY. The place string is the LATIN «Senia, Lika-Korbava megye» and not «Senj», which is why every search of this parish had missed this family
angelika-boras|marriage-of-child|1891|notes/the-kosina-are-filed-under-senia.md|named as mother, «Andelika Boras», at her son Antun's marriage to «Anka Kasuniž» b.1893 — whose own parents the entry gives as «Petar Kasuniž» and «Marija Turina»; ark 1:1:X9D5-MWF2. INDEX ONLY
angelika-boras|marriage-of-child|1919|notes/the-kosina-are-filed-under-senia.md|named as mother, «Andjelika Boras», at her son Pavao's marriage to Anka Blažević; ark 1:1:X9D5-MWXX. INDEX ONLY
mare-luckinic|baptism|1725|notes/the-kosina-are-filed-under-senia.md|Karlobag, 13 April 1725 — INDEX ONLY, «Mare Luckinicha», father «Vicka Luckinicha», no mother named; ark 1:1:QKMX-Y4TT. She was in found.psv as a CANDIDATE sister of ahnentafel 105 from 20 September until 21 September, when publishing blood rather than surnames put her own tree record on the site — born 13 April 1725 to Vicentius Luckinić and Maria, the same day and the same father. The candidate and the person were always the same woman; the archive simply could not see one of them
anton-joanis-uroda|baptism|1780|notes/three-found-people-were-in-the-tree-all-along.md|Karlobag, 13 June 1780 — INDEX ONLY, father «Georgius», mother «Maria». He stood in found.psv as «brother of ahnentafel 54» from 15 September until 21 September, when publishing blood rather than surnames put his own tree record on the site: born the same day to the same parents. Uroda is not one of the eight surnames, which is the only reason he was ever «found» rather than known
maria-rosaria-antic|baptism|1847|notes/three-found-people-were-in-the-tree-all-along.md|Selce, 4 October 1847 — INDEX ONLY, father «Josephus Antic», mother «Maria Jellicic»; ark 3:1:3QS7-899C-596Z-7. She stood in found.psv as «daughter of ahnentafel 24 and 25, sister of ahnentafel 12», and foundcheck settled her on the grounds that «ahnentafel 24 has no children published at all, so there is nothing to match her against». He has one now — her
angelika-boras|baptism|1857|notes/gertruda-exists-in-one-record-in-the-world.md|Senj, 1 September 1857 — INDEX ONLY, «Angelicam Boras», father «Josephi Boras», mother «Mariæ Kabalin»; ark 1:1:QKMJ-SQMC. AGREES WITH THE TREE TO THE DAY
#
# The Kosina, READ FROM THE IMAGES on 21 September 2026. All three scans were
# already in the media library and no page or reading had ever used them.
angelika-boras|marriage|1888|notes/martin-kozina-came-from-carniola.md|Senj marriages p. 209 entry 1, READ FROM THE IMAGE — «1888 dne 12 siečnja», her marriage to «Martin KOZINA, trgovac», age 47, bachelor, whose LOCUS ORIGINIS is «Kranjska župa sv. Martin kod KRAINBURG» — Carniola, the parish of St Martin near Kranj, SLOVENIA. She is «Angjelika Boras», of Senj, age 30. Her parents «Josip Boras, gradski stražar, i Maria rodjena Kabalin». HIS PARENT COLUMN GIVES «Gertruda Kozina, posjednica» AND A DASH WHERE THE FATHER WOULD BE. Witnesses «Mile Crnković, trgovac» and «Ivan Boras, kr. pomorske straže nadstojnik». Celebrant «Mirko Babić, kapelan». Married by dispensation of the Senj Ordinariate, 7 January 1888 no. 38, with the banns read ONCE only
anka-blazevic|marriage|1919|notes/martin-kozina-came-from-carniola.md|Senj marriages p. 359 entry 44, READ FROM THE IMAGE — «1919 studenoga 20», to «Pavao Kosina, trgovac», born 15/III 1894, bachelor. She is «Anka Blažević, radnica u tvornici duhana», born «1893 7/X» — AGREEING WITH THE TREE TO THE DAY — and her LOCUS ORIGINIS IS ENTERED AS «OTOČAC», not Krmpote. Parents «† Martin Kosina i Andjelika r. Boras» and «Juraj Blažević i Tereza r. Žubrinić»; the DAGGER puts Martin's death before November 1919. Witnesses Nikola Sudar and Julije Pavan, trgovci. Celebrant «Luka Malinarić, kapelan»
angelika-boras|marriage-of-child|1919|notes/martin-kozina-came-from-carniola.md|named as the groom's mother TWICE ON ONE PAGE — «Andjelika r. Boras» at entry 44, her son Pavao's marriage of 20 November 1919, and at entry 46, her son Antun's of 24 November. Her husband is daggered in both. Senj marriages p. 359
#
# The two family photographs sent 21 September 2026, read out.
otilija-kosina|grave|1943|notes/otilija-died-in-november-and-neda-was-the-raid.md|Senj, the OTILIJA i NEDA KOSINA stone, read at 4x from photos/line/9000003-otilija-and-neda-kosina-gravestone-senj.jpg — «OTILIJA … čin. Velike župe · ✻1920. †11.11.1943.» Her occupation is činovnica Velike župe, a clerk of the Velika župa. THE DAY THIS ARCHIVE HAD NEVER HAD: 11 November 1943, FIVE WEEKS AFTER THE RAID that killed her father, and the stone does NOT call her a victim of it
neda-kosina|grave|1943|notes/otilija-died-in-november-and-neda-was-the-raid.md|Senj, the same stone, same image read at 4x — «NEDA … maturantica, ŽRTVA ZRAČNOG NAPADA · ✻1924. †7.IX.1943.» A maturantica is a final-year schoolgirl. SHE is the one the stone calls a victim of an air attack, on 7 September 1943 — a month before the October raid, so Senj was bombed more than once. Agrees with the tree's 7 September 1943
antun-anton-kosina|grave|2003|notes/otilija-died-in-november-and-neda-was-the-raid.md|Senj, the same stone, same image read at 4x — «VLČ. ANTE ✻1921 †2003», vlč. for velečasni, Reverend. It confirms in stone that the eldest surviving son was a priest, and it is the same «pop Ante Kosina» who restored Tereza Žubrinić's grave in 1991
oskar-kosina|grave|1954|notes/otilija-died-in-november-and-neda-was-the-raid.md|Senj, the same stone, same image read at 4x — «OSKAR ✻1922 †1954», under «IN MEMORIAM». He is NAMED on his sisters' stone and is not buried under it: he died in Buenos Aires and his memorial card says so. The stone gives the YEAR only and therefore cannot break the card's «4. IV. 1922» against the tree's 4 September
oskar-kosina|death|1954|notes/otilija-died-in-november-and-neda-was-the-raid.md|From his printed memorial card, photos/line/9000002-oskar-kosina-memorial-card-1954.jpg — «OSKAR KOSINA · ✻ 4. IV. 1922. SENJ — HRVATSKA · † 15. I. 1954. BS. AIRES — ARGENTINA». THE DEATH DAY THIS ARCHIVE DID NOT HAVE: 15 January 1954, Buenos Aires. AND A CONFLICT ON HIS BIRTH: the card reads 4. IV. — FOURTH OF APRIL — where the tree says 4 September 1922. IV and IX, Roman four and Roman nine. The stone gives only the year and cannot break the tie
antun-anton-kosina|photograph|1940s|notes/otilija-died-in-november-and-neda-was-the-raid.md|A studio portrait sent by the family 21 September 2026, photos/line/9000001-antun-kosina-priest-portrait.jpg — a young man in a black cassock and a ROMAN COLLAR, head and shoulders, sepia. It is vlč. Ante Kosina in clerical dress, and on the evidence of his age it is close to his ordination, so about the late 1940s. The file WAS NOT in this archive for several hours — shown, read and transcribed, with no image behind the transcription. It was added to the media library the same day as sources/media/local.psv row 9000001
